WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.900
Hey guys, it's Jordan here from Coin Bureau Trading and I'm here with another video on my

00:03.900 --> 00:08.920
favorite indicator which is market cipher. Please make sure you watch the intro video that I dropped

00:08.920 --> 00:13.780
last to get an understanding of all the different parts of this indicator. Now it's time for things

00:13.780 --> 00:18.080
to get exciting and I'm going to look at an actionable trading strategy using the market

00:18.080 --> 00:22.260
cipher indicator. This is the strategy known as wave trend divergences.

00:30.000 --> 00:51.500
After watching the previous setup and intro video your indicator should be looking like mine

00:51.500 --> 00:56.120
on your charts. For the first few examples we're going to keep it quite simple on this daily time

00:56.120 --> 01:00.780
frame it's much easier to understand a new indicator on these higher time frames. Once you

01:00.780 --> 01:06.280
get better at using the indicator and more familiar you can move down to lower time frames depending on

01:06.280 --> 01:12.440
your trading plan and risk appetite. As I explained in the previous market cipher video this blue wave

01:12.440 --> 01:18.740
is your wave trend and these lines between your waves are your divergences. Looking back at some

01:18.740 --> 01:24.740
fairly recent price action for bitcoin on the daily time frame we can see three of these signals did

01:24.740 --> 01:31.520
print. One specific setting I would recommend on this indicator for these wave trend divergences

01:31.520 --> 01:36.940
is to make sure that your wave trend bearish divergence minimum is 45 and your wave trend

01:36.940 --> 01:42.440
bullish divergence minimum is minus 45. For more conservative traders you can put this to 60

01:42.440 --> 01:47.220
and the less conservative traders might want to lower this although I wouldn't recommend it unless

01:47.220 --> 01:53.420
you're highly experienced. On these previous three prints we can clearly see the reaction that we had

01:53.420 --> 02:00.300
in price from these bearish and bullish divergence signals. Again this is a simplification on the

02:00.300 --> 02:05.560
daily time frame but this kind of a strategy can work on lower time frames once you've practiced the

02:05.560 --> 02:10.000
confluence with the other parts of the indicator. If you are trading along with us please do take

02:10.000 --> 02:15.720
advantage of this awesome campaign that we have just for this community from 2bit where you can actually

02:15.720 --> 02:23.920
get free capital for your account just by registering. You can also then double your bonus when you trade

02:23.920 --> 02:32.480
just $1,000 on futures. You can also get an extra $30 bonus just for depositing $100 and these bonuses

02:32.480 --> 02:40.720
increase nicely as your deposit amounts increase all the way up to a $30,000 bonus. Something really

02:40.720 --> 02:45.440
important to understand for this strategy is the confluence needed with the other parts of this

02:45.440 --> 02:51.400
indicator. Let's have a look at this prime example that popped off right here on the 10th of October

02:51.400 --> 02:58.640
in our giant dump on the Trump tariff war news. We can see that just a little bit before around the

02:58.640 --> 03:04.940
7th or 8th of October was when we got our wave trend bearish divergence printed. This is the first sign

03:04.940 --> 03:09.540
that things are looking like a short trade and I would always recommend using the confluence of some

03:09.540 --> 03:15.360
other indicators not just market cipher such as your fixed range volume profile. As many of you know I

03:15.360 --> 03:20.980
really like this indicator. I have a tutorial on it on my personal trading channel if you want to check

03:20.980 --> 03:28.620
it out and we were clearly in the value area high of the range on our fixed range volume profile which

03:28.620 --> 03:33.760
means that we were in a position of power for the short trade. Now we have the go sign on our bearish

03:33.760 --> 03:39.180
divergence and we have the level of confluence with our fixed range volume profile. The two major

03:39.180 --> 03:44.620
levels of confluence that you want to find on your market cipher indicator when trading these

03:44.620 --> 03:52.320
divergences are your VWAP first of all should be crossing down. For those of you who have watched

03:52.320 --> 03:59.240
the intro video will remember that when the VWAP crosses from the upside to the downside this is a

03:59.240 --> 04:05.820
strong reversal signal. We can see here very clearly that in the same daily candle that we printed our

04:05.820 --> 04:13.580
bearish divergence we also received a cross on our VWAP from the upside to the downside. This really is

04:13.580 --> 04:19.820
the second level of confluence here that we want on our bearish wave trend divergence. Looking at price

04:19.820 --> 04:25.400
action candle reading we also had the beautiful bearish engulfing candle coming in. So already that

04:25.400 --> 04:30.800
is a few levels of confluence. We've got our bearish divergence, we've got our VWAP crossing down,

04:30.800 --> 04:36.960
we've got price in our value area high of the range and we have a bearish engulfing candle. The

04:36.960 --> 04:42.340
next important level of confluence that we want and the last one to wait for if it hasn't come in yet

04:42.340 --> 04:49.660
like in this case is our money flow pointing in the same direction as our trade. We can see here in

04:49.660 --> 04:56.580
this instance that as the bearish divergence printed our money flow was still pointing up. This means that

04:56.580 --> 05:02.740
you hold your guns even if you have your VWAP crossing to the downside. Then we can see at the

05:02.740 --> 05:09.420
end of the next daily candle our money flow started to point in in a heavily downward sloping direction.

05:09.820 --> 05:15.720
This really is the ultimate final level of confluence for this strategy and now we had five levels of

05:15.720 --> 05:21.220
confluence. Here we can see what a banger trade this turned out to be even if you entered somewhere in

05:21.220 --> 05:28.780
the next daily candle before the major dip all the way down to a 15% measurable move on bitcoin. Always

05:28.780 --> 05:34.980
be sure to draw in your trades before you enter them. Give yourself a little bit of buffer above your

05:34.980 --> 05:40.000
previous swing high for your stop loss and then make sure you're always bringing your ultimate take

05:40.000 --> 05:46.380
profit down to at least a one to three risk to reward ratio. As I've said before in previous videos

05:46.380 --> 05:52.500
my preference here is to always take your first take profit somewhere around a one to one risk to

05:52.500 --> 06:00.460
reward. So when you have achieved a similar distance to your stop loss into profit in your trade that is

06:00.460 --> 06:06.140
where you can minimize your risk by taking some profit out of the trade. Some conservative traders

06:06.140 --> 06:11.480
will even take their initial margin out of the trade and let their current profit ride further.

06:11.480 --> 06:17.940
Another good strategy here at one to one is to bring your stop loss to a break even so that you are now in a

06:17.940 --> 06:24.200
risk-free trade. On the next bullish divergence we can actually see why this one to one risk to reward risk

06:24.200 --> 06:29.300
managed profit taking strategy is quite a good idea. Here we can see the printing of the bullish divergence.

06:29.560 --> 06:35.840
We can also see that our VWAP crossed to the upside and our money flow was pointing in an upwards direction.

06:35.840 --> 06:41.680
If we drew in and entered this trade somewhere in the next candle after all of these signals printed

06:41.680 --> 06:48.020
with confluence our trade would look something like this with our stop loss below our previous swing low

06:48.020 --> 06:55.120
and our target up at around a one to three risk to reward ratio. Here we can see how powerful the one to

06:55.120 --> 07:01.760
one our profit taking strategy is for risk management and keeping your win rate solid. If we took our first

07:01.760 --> 07:07.140
take profit somewhere similar to the distance between our entry and our stop loss we would have at least

07:07.140 --> 07:13.500
managed our first take profit and our stop loss to break even on this trade making it a profitable

07:13.500 --> 07:18.880
trade. For the less conservative traders who don't put their stop loss to break even we can see you would

07:18.880 --> 07:24.640
have hit your first take profit and now you would be in a little bit of drawdown. At the time of recording

07:24.640 --> 07:30.880
we're not quite sure yet whether this trade will then go to hit stop loss or come back into profit

07:30.880 --> 07:36.400
and go up towards our next take profit targets. Remember to always use Fibonacci retracement

07:36.400 --> 07:44.420
for your profit targets and there is a full video on this on my trading channel. If we start to zoom in

07:44.420 --> 07:49.660
a little bit closer to the four hour time frame we can also see some very nice signals coming in

07:49.660 --> 07:54.740
but the closer you zoom in on the time frame the more experience you need with this indicator and with

07:54.740 --> 08:00.760
risk management in general. Here we saw a very strong bearish divergence print with our VWAP crossing to

08:00.760 --> 08:06.340
the downside and our money flow pointing in a downwards direction. There we saw a very nice trade

08:06.340 --> 08:12.320
moving down through a few take profit levels and actually hitting our final one to three risk to

08:12.320 --> 08:18.580
reward ratio take profit. Although you may have decided to exit this trade when the bullish divergence

08:18.580 --> 08:23.920
signal came in. Here we can see that this bullish divergence was a decent trade that would have given

08:23.920 --> 08:29.340
us the one to one risk to reward ratio but it didn't play out as nicely and this is the warning sign

08:29.340 --> 08:35.640
that we got for that trade not being as ultimate as we might like to see. We did see the bullish

08:35.640 --> 08:42.780
divergence come in and we did see the VWAP crossing to the upside. However our money flow was giving us

08:42.780 --> 08:48.560
a curve that didn't look too convincing that money flow was pointing up. On the other hand here we see

08:48.560 --> 08:53.960
that the next bullish divergence that printed with the VWAP crossing and the money flow pointing up

08:53.960 --> 09:00.380
actually gave us a very decent move to the upside. This move from where it printed had a small amount

09:00.380 --> 09:07.300
of drawdown before moving up to reach our final one to three risk to reward ratio take profit. Even

09:07.300 --> 09:12.340
though this strategy is quite well rounded I would recommend using other drawing tools and indicators

09:12.340 --> 09:19.360
for confluence such as support and resistance, candle patterns, fibonacci, moving averages etc. This strategy

09:19.360 --> 09:24.600
gives us three levels of confluence and as a rule of thumb I would always look for at least five levels

09:24.600 --> 09:30.240
of confluence for a trade in any direction before entering. I hope you've enjoyed this strategy video

09:30.240 --> 09:37.480
please practice on demo and back test using paper trades first and of course always use risk management.

